      "findings": [
        {
          "finding": "The fact the per-record check is safe because of: each record's own range ends at the nearest later base of any record at HEAD, so the records at HEAD split the check range into ranges that do not overlap, and a commit no changed record holds fails the check. The stack fixture test proves it, and three mutations (end every range at HEAD, pool coverage across records, drop the uncovered-commit check) each make it fail.",
          "cites": "Steps 2",
          "none": "Logs are in pr5e-evidence/ at the PR 5e worktree root."
        },
        {
          "finding": "Where grep stops: verify.cjs runs skills:check only as a range check, and hosted CI runs verify:current without --base, so the per-record check runs in verify:commit but not in hosted CI. The repository needs no change for this. The workflow change is in work/skill-process-evidence/ci-range-checks.patch for the owner, and L2 in skill-process-4 stays open until it lands.",
          "cites": "Steps 3",
          "none": "The fix is the owner-applied CI patch, not a repository change."
        },
        {
          "finding": "Under the per-record rule, the skill-process-3 review entries for blast-radius and principle-prove-it-works hold only receipts that agent ad1b4f1b47d1a5c1a made on 9f62d28, which is below record 3's base fb66468, so the check rejects them. I did not edit them.",
          "cites": "Steps 4",
          "open": "A fresh reviewer re-records the skill-process-3 review."
        }
      ],
